  "name": null,
  "problem": "Find the $y$-intercept of $\\overset{\u2194}{AB},$ and express the equation of this line in slope-intercept form.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The $y$-intercept of the line is $b\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        The equation is $y\\,=\\,$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}",
  "worked_solution": "We will write the equation of the line in the slope-intercept form \n\n$$\ny=mx+b.\n$$\n\nAs we found previously, the slope is $m=-3.$\n\nSubstituting $m=-3$ into the slope-intercept form above, we get\n\n$$\ny=-3x+b.\n$$\n\nWe now need to find the $y$-intercept $b.$ We can find this by substituting the coordinates of a point on the line. Any point will do, so let's substitute $(3,-2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =-3x+b \\\\ -2 & =-3(3)+b \\\\ -2 & =-9+b \\\\ 7 & =b \\\\ b & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the line is \n\n$$\ny=-3x+7.\n$$",
